Jesse Vincent. The full upstream license text is in LICENSE-superpowers;
modifications are by Lowell Mason and released under the same MIT terms.

Changes from upstream:
  - Cross-skill references rewritten from the `superpowers:` plugin
    namespace to bare skill names (these install as standalone personal
    skills, not as a namespaced plugin).
  - Skill-authoring scaffolding removed (creation log, pressure-test
    transcripts) where it was not referenced at runtime.
  - The `using-superpowers` plugin-bootstrap skill was dropped.
  - agents/code-reviewer.md is a read-only agent definition distilled from
    the adapted requesting-code-review reviewer template (same MIT terms).
  - agents/task-reviewer.md is a read-only agent definition distilled from
    the adapted subagent-driven-development task-reviewer template (same
    MIT terms).
  - brainstorming's visual-companion server no longer fetches the upstream
    remote brand image or carries telemetry toggles; the attribution link
    to github.com/obra/superpowers remains.
  - The planning/execution skills (brainstorming, writing-plans,
    executing-plans, subagent-driven-development) were extended with a
    spec-driven lifecycle not present upstream: specs/ and specs/plans/
    conventions plus a plan-completion protocol (plan markup, a
    deferred-items log, spec/plan retirement).

